{"id": "EUVD-2026-67510", "enisaUuid": "c3e9217a-3586-383a-9e4d-e3ad0173a351", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: flowtable: avoid num_encaps underflow on bridge VLAN untag\n\nThe DEV_PATH_BR_VLAN_UNTAG case post-decrements info->num_encaps\ninside WARN_ON_ONCE(). num_encaps is u8, so if it's already 0 the\ndecrement still happens and wraps it to 255. The break only leaves\nthe inner switch -- a later path entry can set info->indev back to\na real device, and we end up returning with num_encaps == 255.\n\nnft_dev_forward_path() then walks info.encap[] (size 2) up to\nnum_encaps, which means an OOB stack read and a bogus count copied\ninto the route descriptor.\n\nShould only happen on a malformed bridge path stack, hence the WARN,\nbut worth handling sanely. Move the decrement out of the WARN.\n\n[ While at this, remove the WARN_ON_ONCE since this can only happen\n  with a buggy bridge path stack --pablo ].", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:48:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:46:41", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1b52aeb40c9f04bf50eeb4ea09142139d163e239", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee8440bb000fff4ef8acbfc99652851e9ca0a35b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/547ea9f567498e4accc89e7816264f15a1a0629f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2f55fa28011c97d6495d5787808db10a8c2d690d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e052f920773b73be49eb4d8702a9f85de7464363"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80634", "GHSA-jm3q-xwgv-hgh8"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.67, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "189be55d-102e-3b28-b06a-d9d1752f46ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e990cef6516daa4e1e236433579e333f74fd38cb <1b52aeb40c9f04bf50eeb4ea09142139d163e239"}, {"id": "1d9c0d6a-195d-39a4-90d6-2b1773b8ef41", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e990cef6516daa4e1e236433579e333f74fd38cb <ee8440bb000fff4ef8acbfc99652851e9ca0a35b"}, {"id": "26efdd18-4334-3919-9f65-b87adc48162d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.13"}, {"id": "41341428-2a75-3be3-9f21-47156f8ddb7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "55169e83-a095-395e-8062-ccce34e27599", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e990cef6516daa4e1e236433579e333f74fd38cb <e052f920773b73be49eb4d8702a9f85de7464363"}, {"id": "72f4bfed-ce87-35d2-b661-a59c6a1c9a05", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e990cef6516daa4e1e236433579e333f74fd38cb <547ea9f567498e4accc89e7816264f15a1a0629f"}, {"id": "789befd1-bb74-37e3-82f7-d34ca3f4c07f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7b0b25e0-a9ed-3536-a07a-add8f100838a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e990cef6516daa4e1e236433579e333f74fd38cb <2f55fa28011c97d6495d5787808db10a8c2d690d"}, {"id": "9b04b8d9-852d-3533-8612-d37a9fe167c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "bfeb0974-ad39-3892-9eb6-d927f4070c29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "c3442029-6814-3189-876c-a0963cf32cbc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "f8f89b1b-7e88-3a54-b265-3574c408c7ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "87bbf0cd-adbb-3710-9526-39d5f4c923b5", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}